--- Finding (distance_and_bearing): a parameter named like a function of the program is
--- accepted, and an index of it is read as a CALL of the function: the modes disagree.
---
--- crow run -i:  prints 0 — `scores[0]` in `first` calls the function scores with 0
---               (0 * 2), a silent wrong answer: the list handed in is never read.
--- crow run:     error[E0618]: expected function, found `CrowTensor` (src/main.rs)
---               "the compiled program does not build — … a bug in Crow"
--- Expected: 5 in both modes, or a refusal at the parameter (spec, Names Are Never
--- Ambiguous: "a bare name in Crow means exactly one thing. Collisions are never
--- resolved silently — not by shadowing"; its example is exactly this one, an index read
--- as a call). A parameter only used in arithmetic (`fn twice[scores]` / `return
--- scores * 2`) gives 42 in both modes, so the collision passes unnoticed until the
--- parameter is indexed. Met writing `fn row[name, distance, bearing]` beside
--- `fn distance[...]` and `fn bearing[...]` (worked around by renaming).
fn scores[x]
    return x * 2

fn first[scores]
    return scores[0]

log[first[[5, 6]]]
